{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210733,"nonce":"solm+c0GBD+40fESKgXFkZAm7fk=","title":"AOT subscript on FORWARDED receiver after GC","message":"Fixed in commit 8979286. Record migrated from session memory 2026-09-12.\n\n\n| Commit | What | Mac effect | Linux Docker effect |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `2da4613` | FP-chain forwarding fixup in `collect_garbage` (runtime, scans AOT frames for FORWARDED slots) | dies at req 2 → 60/60 OK | instant SEGV → 22-27/30 OK |\n| `a06926c` | Root saved `JitContext.closure`/`defining_class` across `poll()` in `wlift_aot_invoke_sm_method` | unchanged | unchanged |\n| `1d6a30a` | Bump Cranelift 0.130 → 0.133 via `[patch.crates-io]` → `github.com/darmie/wasmtime#fix/cranelift-object-darwin-platform`. Picks up upstream `decb45f` (variable defs in stack maps) + `24938c4163` (alias values in `rewrite_use`). Adds wren_lift declarations of `current_resume_v_var` and SM dispatch-block BlockParam load results. | top patch site 107→24 | same |\n| `8f4267c` | **The real fix**: declare SM-transform fresh ValueIds as stack-map roots at all four SM-load sites (`resume_loads` in CrossFnCallResume, `resume_loads` in DirectYield Branch, `direct_yield_results` binding, `cross_fn_results` slot-reload). Drops the `is_wren_value` gate that was filtering them out. | **0 patches needed, FP-fixup OFF → 60/60 OK in 5/5, 80/80 mixed stress** | partial — same gap categories remain |\n\n\nThe SM transform allocates fresh `ValueId`s via `mir.new_value()` for each saved-across-yield slot (`resume_loads`, `direct_yield_results`, `cross_fn_results`). These vids appear ONLY in the `StateMachineLayout` metadata — **never** as `BlockParam` or `Instruction` defs in any MIR block.\n\n`infer_osr_value_types` walks `mir.blocks` to populate `value_types`. SM-only vids aren't referenced from any block's instructions, so their entry stays at the default `MirType::Void`. The `is_wren_value(fresh_vid, \u0026value_types)` gate at the four SM load sites then returned **false**, skipping `declare_value_needs_stack_map`.\n\nWithout the declaration:\n- Cranelift's safepoint pass leaves the loaded value un-spilled.\n- Regalloc keeps the value in a callee-saved register across all subsequent safepoints.\n- Every use reads the register directly with no `ldr` from a stack slot.\n- After a GC fires, the slot (in the stack map) gets the forwarded pointer, but the register cached the pre-GC value.\n- The mutator resumes reading the stale register → use-after-move → \"Subscript N out of bounds (count 0)\" / null-deref SEGV.\n\nThe four SM load sites all produce Wren Values by construction (runtime call returns + fiber's `resume_v` parameter, both u64-encoded NaN-boxed). The `is_wren_value` gate was wrong; the declaration is always correct.\n\nDisassembly confirms the fix: before, the third+ `sm_load_value` calls returned into x24/x26 with no spill; after, every `wlift_aot_sm_load_value` result is followed by `stur x0, [sp, #N]`, and post-safepoint uses go through `ldur` reloads.\n\n\n1. **Minimal CLIF repro** at [cranelift/filetests/filetests/isa/aarch64/safepoint-reload-eliminated.clif](cranelift/filetests/filetests/isa/aarch64/safepoint-reload-eliminated.clif). Confirms Cranelift's safepoint pass works correctly when values are properly declared — the bug was on wlift's side, not Cranelift's.\n\n2. **CLIF-level investigation branch** `fix/safepoint-spill-load-elimination` in the wasmtime fork (local-only). Initially aimed at fixing Cranelift's late-stage optimizer collapsing reloads back into register reads — turned out unnecessary once we found the wlift-side gate.\n\n3. **Cranelift-object Darwin platform fix** in fork branch `fix/cranelift-object-darwin-platform`. Independent issue needed to unblock macOS testing.\n\n\n- gpu/api 30-request alternation: **30/30 OK in 5/5 trials**, 0 aborts\n- gpu/api 60-request: **60/60 OK in 5/5 trials**\n- 80-request mixed-endpoint stress: **80/80 OK**\n- Spec corpus: **41/41 PASS**\n- cargo test lib: **923 PASS**\n- cargo test aot_runtime: **21 PASS**\n- cargo test e2e: 112/113 (1 pre-existing osr flake, unrelated)\n\nThe FP-chain fixup at `VM::conservative_fp_chain_forward_fixup` is now defensive-only on Mac — the runtime workaround can stay in tree but is no longer load-bearing.\n\n\nBoth Mac and Linux Docker show the **same 9 stack-map gaps** under `WLIFT_VALIDATE_STACKMAP=1`:\n\n| Function | Offsets |\n|---|---|\n| `wlift_aot_main` (post-`App.listen` tail) | +18248 |\n| `wlift_aot_mod_9__closure_0..8` | +1372, +2960, +1232, +1232, +11552 |\n| `wlift_aot_mod_9__method_4_1`, `4_2` | +508, +2744, +3196 |\n\n\nEvery gap traces to the **return offset of `wlift_aot_invoke_sm_method`** — the cross-fn SM invoke helper. The IR pattern at each site (`closure_5 +1232`, `method_4_1 +508`, `closure_8 +11552`, etc.) is identical:\n\n```clif\nv_recv = call wlift_aot_sm_load_arg(fiber, 0), stack_map=[…]\n…\nv_ret = call wlift_aot_invoke_sm_method(vm, fiber, v_recv, sym, narg, resume_v)   ; NO stack_map=\nstack_store v_ret, ss0\nv_kind = call wlift_aot_sm_peek_poll_kind(), stack_map=[i64 @ ss0+0]\n```\n\nThe args (`v_recv`, `resume_v`, user args) were ALREADY saved into the child fiber's frame slots via `wlift_aot_sm_save_arg` before the invoke. The runtime's GC walker handles child frame slots independently. After `invoke_sm_method` returns, only the result value is needed — and it's immediately spilled to ss0 which becomes the stack-map root at the next safepoint. So at the invoke call site, no AOT-side Wren Value needs the stack map.\n\nMac empirically confirms: 60/60 + 80/80 mixed stress + 41/41 specs on this exact code with these exact gaps. Cranelift's safepoint pass correctly omits stack_map= when there are no live declared roots — that's the design, not a bug.\n\n\n**Root cause**: `collect_garbage`'s native-stack writeback loop guarded each spill slot against a fixed `USER_VA_LIMIT = 1usize \u003c\u003c 47` ceiling. Linux aarch64 under Docker on Apple Silicon hands out stack pages in `0xffff_xxxx_xxxx` — perfectly valid userspace memory in the container's VA layout, but above 1\u003c\u003c47. Every writeback into those slots was silently dropped.\n\nThe GC walker still correctly identified the live roots, called `update_value_inline` on the in-memory `roots` Vec, and chased the FORWARDED markers to their new old-gen locations. It just never wrote the updated bits back to the actual stack slot. So when the AOT code resumed and re-loaded the receiver via `ldur x0, [sp, #N]`, it read the pre-promote pointer. `wren_subscript_get` then dereferenced the FORWARDED source, whose `forget_heap_on_source` had set `count = 0`, and ran into the `validate_index` arm that produces `Subscript {0..9} out of bounds (count 0)`.\n\nThe diagnostic that pinpointed this:\n- Gated dump in `wren_subscript_get` (`WLIFT_TRACE_STALE_SUBSCRIPT=1`): when `gc_mark == FORWARDED` on receipt, walks the native FP chain via dladdr and prints each AOT frame's symbol+offset, plus the topmost frame's safepoint live_roots and the actual bits at each tracked slot.\n- That dump showed the receiver's NaN-boxed value sitting in a slot that WAS listed in `live_roots[7]` of the safepoint metadata — meaning the GC walker visited it but the writeback didn't land.\n- Then `WLIFT_GC_TRACE_WRITEBACK=1` (extended to count VA-limit-skips) produced `WARNING: skipped 62 stack-root writebacks because slot addr \u003e= USER_VA_LIMIT (1\u003c\u003c47); sample first slot addr=0xffffdae7fc68`.\n\n**Fix**: drop the `addr \u003e= USER_VA_LIMIT` check on the writeback path. Keep `addr != 0` and `addr \u0026 7 == 0` — that's the actual safety envelope. The slot addresses come from the FP chain we just walked, not from untrusted input, so a stricter bound buys nothing.\n\n**Did NOT touch**: the `USER_VA_LIMIT` check in the suspended-fiber krio-stack scan. Removing it there caused one SIGBUS in 3 `hatch-http/http` spec runs on Mac — the suspended-fiber walk follows whatever was saved when the fiber yielded, which is a less-trustworthy input than the live FP chain. Left that path alone.\n\n**Results post-fix**:\n- Mac: 60/60 gpu URL alternation, 41/41 specs, 923/21/113 lib/aot/e2e tests — unchanged.\n- Linux Docker: 5/5 trials × 30/30 OK, plus 120/120 mixed-endpoint stress (gpu page, gpu/api, /, /healthz). Was 0/5 SIGSEGV pre-`8f4267c`, then 5/5 container-stable with 5-8 fiber aborts post-`8f4267c`, now clean 5/5 × 30/30 plus stress.\n\nThe diagnostic infrastructure (`WLIFT_TRACE_STALE_SUBSCRIPT`, the dladdr-based AOT frame dump, the VA-limit skip counter in `WLIFT_GC_TRACE_WRITEBACK`) stays in tree. Zero cost when env vars unset; ready to go for any future stale-pointer hunt.\n\n\nBranch `fix/cranelift-object-darwin-platform` at `github.com/darmie/wasmtime` is ready for an upstream PR. Contains the Darwin → PLATFORM_MACOS mapping needed for `ld64` to accept the emitted .o files on macOS hosts. The wlift bug fix is entirely wlift-side; the upstream `decb45f` + `24938c4163` (already on main) cover the Cranelift side.\n\n\n- `WLIFT_AOT_FP_FIXUP=0` — opt out of the FP-chain fixup (use to bisect / measure overhead)\n- `WLIFT_AOT_FP_FIXUP_TRACE=1` — dump per-GC counters + per-patch `caller_fn=... call_after=+N slot=@fp{:+}` lines\n- `WLIFT_VALIDATE_STACKMAP=1` — log candidate stack-map gaps at every GC\n- `WLIFT_VALIDATE_STACKMAP=strict` — panic on first gap\n- `WLIFT_AOT_GC=0` — disable AOT GC entirely (no nursery, no FORWARDED, no bug — but RSS grows unbounded)\n- `WLIFT_AOT_DUMP_FN=NAME` — dump SM-transformed MIR + layout for a specific function (used during this investigation)","files":null}]}